  "summary": "Senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore of the Nick Xenophon Team (NXT) has announced her resignation from the Australian Senate after discovering she holds British citizenship by descent through her mother, who was born in Singapore when it was a British colony. Despite previously believing she was not a British citizen based on past embassy advice, recent confirmation from the UK Home Office and a specialist barrister revealed her status. Kakoschke-Moore expressed shock and heartbreak over the revelation. She plans to refer the vacancy to the High Court for determination, with a possible recount of the 2016 Senate election potentially leading to the election of NXT candidate Tim Storrer. Party leader Nick Xenophon expressed sadness over her departure but remains hopeful for her political return, noting legal uncertainty about filling the vacancy due to a recent High Court ruling involving Hollie Hughes."
}
```

